# What belongs in this repository: the pipeline, the notebooks, the config,
# the audit scripts. Everything else here is either downloaded, generated, or
# borrowed, and all of it can be rebuilt from what is tracked.

# --- Satellite data ---------------------------------------------------------
# The HSD cache normally lives outside the repo (paths.cache_dir in config.yml
# defaults to C:/himawari_cache), but ignore it here too in case someone points
# it inside. A three-day run is ~78 GB.
himawari_cache/
*.DAT
*.DAT.bz2
*.part

# --- Generated output -------------------------------------------------------
# frames/ reached 6.8 GB for one three-day run; output/ holds the encoded video.
# The glob matters: examples/tonga.yml writes to frames_tonga/, and any other
# run pointed at frames_<name>/ would otherwise be committed as loose PNGs.
frames/
frames_*/
output/
output_*/
temp/

# --- Third-party reference code --------------------------------------------
# Clones of other people's repositories, kept locally for reading. They have
# their own upstreams and their own licences; they are not ours to redistribute.
references/

# --- Credentials ------------------------------------------------------------
.env

# --- Notebooks --------------------------------------------------------------
# Executed notebooks embed their output images as base64 and grow enormous:
# 02_process.ipynb is ~42 MB after a full run against ~15 KB of actual source.
# Strip outputs before committing:  python tools/nbstrip.py notebook/*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- Content Support ---------------------------------------------------------
blog/
audit/
tools/
#docs/

# --- One-off maintenance ----------------------------------------------------
# Re-renders every product in place. It existed to restamp frames produced
# before the observation-time fix; a first run already writes correct
# timestamps, so a new user has no use for it.
examples/rerender_all.py

# --- CLAUDE ----------------------------------------------------
HANDOFF.md